---
components: ["RadialProgress"]
description: Radial progress shows a value on a circular, three-quarter, or half arc, with room for a number in the center.
---

<script>
  import { Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { DeltaIndicator, RadialProgress } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const thresholds = [
    { value: 80, kind: "warning" },
    { value: 95, kind: "error" },
  ];
</script>

`RadialProgress` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

A bar is easier to compare than an arc. Reach for this when a single value needs presence, such as on a KPI card, and use [BulletChart](/components/BulletChart) or [ShareOfTotal](/components/ShareOfTotal) inside tables.

## Basic

Pass a `value` and a `label`. The scale runs from `min` to `max`, 0 to 100 by default. The center shows the share of the scale.

<RadialProgress value={72} label="Disk usage" />

## Arcs

Set `arc` to `"full"`, `"three-quarter"`, or `"half"`. The open arcs read as gauges.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={7}>
  <RadialProgress value={72} label="Full" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} arc="three-quarter" label="Three quarter" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} arc="half" label="Half" />
</Stack>

## Thresholds

Set `thresholds` to status levels. The arc takes the color of the highest one the value has reached, and each is drawn as a tick across the track, so status never rests on color alone. The shape is the same one [Meter](/components/Meter) takes, including the `{ warning, error }` object.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={7}>
  <RadialProgress value={62} {thresholds} arc="three-quarter" label="Disk usage" />
  <RadialProgress value={86} {thresholds} arc="three-quarter" label="Disk usage" />
  <RadialProgress value={97} thresholds={{ warning: 80, error: 95 }} arc="three-quarter" label="Disk usage" />
</Stack>

`threshold` fires when an update moves the value across a threshold. It never fires on mount. The detail holds the `threshold`, the `direction`, and the new `value`.

## Center

`format` takes `Intl.NumberFormat` options or a function, and is given the value rather than the share. Set `hideValue` for a bare arc, or fill the default slot with anything. The slot receives `value`, `ratio`, `formattedValue`, and `status`.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={7}>
  <RadialProgress value={412} max={512} format={(value) => `${value} GB`} label="Storage" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} hideValue label="Bare" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} diameter={128} label="Completion" let:formattedValue>
    <div>
      <div class="bx--type-productive-heading-04">{formattedValue}</div>
      <DeltaIndicator value={0.04} format="percent" size="sm" />
    </div>
  </RadialProgress>
</Stack>

## Size

Set `diameter` in pixels. `thickness` defaults to an eighth of it.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={7}>
  <RadialProgress value={72} diameter={32} hideValue label="32 pixels" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} diameter={64} label="64 pixels" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} diameter={128} thickness={6} label="Thin" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} diameter={128} thickness={24} label="Thick" />
</Stack>

## Color

Set `color` to a semantic name, a categorical index from 1 to 14, a viz token name, or any CSS color. A reached threshold wins.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={7}>
  <RadialProgress value={72} color="success" label="Success" />
  <RadialProgress value={72} color={3} label="Categorical" />
</Stack>

## Accessibility

With a `label`, the graphic has the `meter` role with the value, the scale, and the formatted value as its text. Without a label it is hidden from assistive technology. The arc mirrors in a right to left layout.
